# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime state - never commit these.
#
# These are matched anywhere in the tree, not just under apps/api, because the
# API resolves PGLITE_DIR and STORAGE_DIR relative to the process working
# directory. Starting the server from the repo root (which is what Render does)
# puts them at the root instead of inside apps/api, and an anchored-only rule
# silently fails to match - which is how a PGlite database and the seeded asset
# blobs ended up in git history once already.
#
#   .data/     embedded Postgres data directory
#   storage/   uploaded asset blobs (local stand-in for S3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.data/
storage/
**/.data/
**/storage/

# Postgres lock/pid files, belt and braces.
*.pid
postmaster.pid

# Never commit real secrets - .env.example is the tracked template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Screenshots from apps/web/scripts/shoot-mobile.mjs - local review artefacts.
.screens/
